Package: seg
Version: 0.6-0
Date: 2026-11-08
Title: Measuring Spatial Segregation
Authors@R: c(
    person("Seong-Yun", "Hong", email = "syhong@khu.ac.kr",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("David", "O'Sullivan", role = "aut"),
    person("Benjamin", "Jarvis", role = "ctb",
           comment = "scaled kernels in localenv()"),
    person("Changlock", "Choi", role = "ctb"))
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: sf (>= 1.0-24), splancs, graphics, grDevices, stats
Description: Measuring spatial segregation. The methods implemented in this
    package include White's P index (1983) <doi:10.1086/227768>,
    Morrill's D(adj) (1991), Wong's D(w) and D(s) (1993)
    <doi:10.1080/00420989320080551>, and Reardon and O'Sullivan's set of
    spatial segregation measures (2004)
    <doi:10.1111/j.0081-1750.2004.00150.x>, with maps of where segregation
    is strong or weak. Spatial data are handled with 'sf'.
License: GPL (>= 3)
